<%# WHAT THEY TOLD HIM TO PREPARE, read back out of their own mail.

   Closed, like every other section on this page. The count on the summary is
   what says there is something in here; the passages themselves are a page of
   somebody else's mail, and they belong to a round that is usually weeks off.
   Nothing here is typed — the passages are found in the beats, so the section
   appears when a mail actually asked for something and not otherwise. See
   InterviewAsks.

   Each one says which round it is FOR, because that is the whole question with
   a rundown of four rounds sent in one mail at the start: not what they asked
   for, but which conversation they asked for it in.

   NOTHING IN THE HEAD IS A STATUS. The chip is which mail the ask came out of
   and the round beside it is one nobody has booked yet, so both are drawn
   hollow — a filled chip on this page means the application IS there, and an
   availability request that read as a booked interview is the one thing this
   panel must not say. %>
<% if asks.any? %>
  <details class="job-details job-asks">
    <summary>
      What they asked you to prepare
      <span class="count"><%= asks.size %></span>
    </summary>

    <ul class="ask-list">
      <% asks.each do |ask| %>
        <li>
          <div class="ask-head">
            <%= link_to "##{ask.note.id}", "#note-#{ask.note.id}", class: "ask-beat",
                  title: "The beat it arrived in" %>
            <span class="note-tag note-tag-<%= ask.note.tag %>"><%= ask.note.tag_label %></span>
            <span class="note-when">
              <%= ask.occurred_at.strftime("%b %-d, %Y") %>
            </span>
            <% ask.round_labels.each do |round| %>
              <span class="ask-round">for the <%= round.downcase %></span>
            <% end %>
          </div>

          <%# Verbatim, and printed the way a beat's body is - the indentation
             and the bullets are how the instruction was written, and HTML
             collapses both on sight. %>
          <div class="note-body"><%= note_body(ask.said) %></div>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
  </details>
<% end %>
